## Knight's tour (knights-tour), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   4. If a clear location is movable from a captured location then you can move a red block onto the clear location and move an available clear blue block onto the captured location.
##   5. If a block is not on a location then it is available.
##   6. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   7. If a location is below a red block then it is captured.
##   8. If a location that is alongside a captured location is diagonal with an object that is not next to the captured location then the object is movable from the captured location.
##  11. The goal is that all locations are covered.
##  13. If a location is below an object then it is covered.
## World: init-atour2.world (a 4 by 3 grid; the red block on one location, eleven blue blocks in a stack)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator tour-move (argument1 = the red block, argument2 = the clear location), statement 4. captured (statement 7) is
##     expanded in place (the location below the red block); movable-from (statement 8) is the knight's move, a static
##     relation computed from alongside, diagonal-with and near as in knight swapping (A-S3).
##   - "The solution has eleven steps" (statement 9) is checked against the plans, not used.
##   - available (not on a location) and clear are maintained one-argument relations; the blue blocks start in a stack, and the
##     clear available blue block is its top, found by the applications (A-G4).
##   - covered (below an object) is expanded in place; the goal is expanded over the locations of the world file.

## Propose initialize-knights-tour when its conditions below hold.
sp {knights-tour*propose*initialize-knights-tour
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-knights-tour ^task-operator false)
}

sp {knights-tour*apply*initialize-knights-tour
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-knights-tour ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name knights-tour ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <o-location-1> <o-location-2> <o-location-3> <o-location-4> <o-location-5> <o-location-6> <o-location-7> <o-location-8> <o-location-9> <o-location-10> <o-location-11> <o-location-12> <o-block-13> <o-block-14> <o-block-15> <o-block-16> <o-block-17> <o-block-18> <o-block-19> <o-block-20> <o-block-21> <o-block-22> <o-block-23> <o-block-24> <o-task>)
